During the 1977–78 Scottish football season, [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] competed in the [[Scottish Premier Division]].

Despite not achieving any major honour this season, Celtic played the [[List of Scottish League Cup finals|Scottish League Cup Final]] for the 14th season in a row, which is still a record as of 2025. No other team has played more than 5 League Cup Finals in a row.

This was the club's last season under manager [[Jock Stein]], and the first season in which [[Danny McGrain]] was captain.

